{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #611: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. For a graph $G$ let $\\tau(G)$ denote the minimal number of vertices that include at least one from each maximal clique of $G$ (sometimes called the clique transversal number).\n\nIs it true that if all maximal cliques in $G$ have at least $cn$ vertices then $\\tau(G)=o_c(n)$?\n\nSimilarly, estimate for $c>0$ the minimal $k_c(n)$ such that if every maximal clique in $G$ has at least $k_c(n)$ vertices then $\\tau(G)<(1-c)n$. Prize: no. Tags: graph theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_7689bd3513a7c1874548972dcfcd2f3ab852b18a983243cee36e21c833445df0","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:611","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_1a36bacf89428de3","object_root":"sha256:5f3b42c9372f5c5f3ef3141e9b39424ded2bea14c4ae5728ad534415e36c91c4","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:611"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"vela.claim-record.v1"}